WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.155
Your course is a content engine.

00:00:02.155 --> 00:00:04.309
One lesson can become several Shorts.

00:00:04.309 --> 00:00:07.542
This lesson is about repurpose one lesson into shorts.

00:00:07.542 --> 00:00:08.978
Course as content engine.

00:00:08.978 --> 00:00:11.492
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.492 --> 00:00:15.083
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.083 --> 00:00:20.470
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.420
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:29.448
Stay practical: cut three hooks from one lesson before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.768 --> 00:00:35.009
Cut three hooks from one lesson: a tension line, a rule, and a next action.

00:00:35.009 --> 00:00:38.153
Remember the objective: cut three hooks from one lesson.

00:00:38.153 --> 00:00:41.996
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.996 --> 00:00:46.188
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:46.188 --> 00:00:50.032
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.032 --> 00:00:54.224
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.544 --> 00:00:57.476
Keep each clip under a short attention window.

00:00:57.476 --> 00:00:58.942
One idea per clip.

